       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The current FDA-approved label for amlodipine lists 10 mg once daily as the maximum, so 50 mg is well above it. I can't verify the claim that the label allows 50 mg, and it doesn't match the label as I know it. This patient has normal kidney and liver function and no other factors that would justify a dose this high.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg** once daily. Tell me which and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Talk to pharmacy or the prescriber of record.** If there's an unusual indication I don't know about, they can review it. They can also enter the order through their own override process.\n- **Add more blood pressure control** if 10 mg isn't enough. I can enter a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, if you give me the drug and dose."
